# NixOS Environment Initialization

This project relies on a Nix development shell to provide core tools like `pnpm`, `node`, and `npx`. They are not installed globally on this system.

Whenever you need to execute a terminal command for the first time in a session, you MUST first enter the development shell by running:
`source ~/.bashrc && dev carsons`

Wait for the shell prompt to change or load. Once you are inside the `dev carsons` shell, you can execute `pnpm`, `npx`, and other build commands normally. 

If a command fails with "command not found: pnpm", you forgot to enter the Nix shell.
